  "principles": [
    "Start with the smallest skill that owns the immediate output.",
    "Use routers for broad domains and specialists for detailed execution.",
    "Keep cross-references short; detailed rules live in the owning skill.",
    "Use MCPs only for live data, app, service, or tool boundaries.",
    "Respect current user authorization and host policy for external, paid, destructive, credential or bulk actions; skill routing grants no new authority.",
    "Maintain methods in personal plugin sources; never edit installed caches.",
    "Compatibility entrypoints are disabled; their direct file links resolve the current owner.",
    "Use platform/tool providers on demand; do not create an environment for markdown routing.",
    "Name entrypoints for a capability or action, without vendor superlatives; add a new head for a distinct recurring workflow or different tools/validation, and keep method depth in conditional references.",
    "Prefer the existing plugin owner; split independent use cases into focused skills. Target 8–10 diverse workflows without padding and preserve full source methods/support rather than summaries."
